Movie Details Lookup
Problem Statement
Your cousin is a huge movie and TV fan. They often forget when a movie came out or who starred in it, 
so they want a simple webpage where they can type a movie or series name and instantly see its details.

The page should let them enter a movie or series name, click a Search button, and view the main details for that one title on the screen.

You will use a real public API to fetch this information.

API Information
You must use the OMDb API (The Open Movie Database).

Website & documentation: http://www.omdbapi.com/
You need to register on the website to get your own API key.
Before you start coding, open the documentation page and figure out:

Which URL parameter lets you search by exact title (for one movie/series).
How to include your API key in the URL.
Which JSON fields you want to show (for example: title, year, type, poster, rating, plot).
Testing and Debugging
To fully understand the challenge, you should follow these two steps:

Use Postman to learn how the API behaves
Send a test request to the API endpoint.
Check the response to understand which fields you will receive.
This helps you understand what your request and response will look like before writing any code.
Build and test your project locally
Write your code on your local computer using an index.html and script.js file.
Open your HTML file in the browser to test your interface and API calls.
Use DevTools effectively:
Sources tab: to debug your JavaScript step by step and inspect variables.
Network tab: to see each request your page makes, what data was sent, and what response came back.


Your Task
Create a webpage with:
An input box where the user can type a movie or series name.
A Search button.
A details section that already contains separate elements for each piece of information:
One element to display the title.
One element to display the year.
One element to display the type.
One element to display the IMDb rating.
One element (such as a div) to hold the poster image.
One element to display the plot summary.
An area to display error messages.
When the page first loads:
The details elements should be empty.
The error area should be empty.
No API call is made automatically.
When the user clicks the Search button:
Read the text from the input box and trim extra spaces.
Clear any old details and error messages.
If the input is empty, show an error message such as: "Please enter a movie or series name." and do not call the API.
If there is a title, use it to make an API call to the OMDb API using fetch().
After the API response:
If the movie or series is not found, show an error message such as: "Movie or series not found." and leave the details elements empty.
If the data is valid, fill the details elements for one movie or series with exactly:
Title
Year
Type (movie/series)
Poster image, or a message saying "No poster available" if the value is "N/A"
IMDb rating
Plot summary
Error handling:
Any error during the fetch process, such as network issues or unexpected JSON structure, 
should be shown in the error area instead of leaving the page blank or broken. The details elements should be cleared when this happens.
